microtun for Debian
===================

This package installs both Linux executables:

  /usr/bin/microtun
  /usr/bin/microtun-tracker

The Tracker service is installed as microtun-tracker.service, but package
installation deliberately does not enable or start it. The packaged
/etc/microtun/tracker.toml is an example and must be reviewed before first use.
It contains a private tunnel key placeholder and should remain readable only by
root and the dedicated microtun-tracker service group.

After configuring the Tracker:

  systemctl enable --now microtun-tracker.service
  systemctl status microtun-tracker.service

The package creates a dedicated microtun-tracker system user and group for the
service. The service does not run as root.

The microtun executable is intentionally not installed as a system-wide service:
a Linux host may have multiple device configurations and interface names. A
sample device configuration is installed at:

  /usr/share/doc/microtun/examples/device.toml

For example:

  microtun -i mtun0 /path/to/device.toml
